# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Frontend build-time variables (Next.js)
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined into the JS bundle when the app is BUILT, not read
# at runtime. These belong in the build environment of whatever deploys the
# three Next apps (Vercel project settings, or Docker build args) — putting
# them only in a running container's env has no effect, and changing one
# requires a rebuild, not a restart.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Public storefront URL. REQUIRED: admin-ui and seller-ui build their
# "View product" links from it. Unset, those links resolve relative to the
# dashboard's own host and 404.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_USER_UI_LINK=https://<storefront-domain>

# Google Maps. Set the provider to "google" ONLY once the key is present and
# restricted (HTTP referrer + Maps JavaScript, Places and Geocoding APIs only);
# the key is public once it is in the bundle. Leaving the provider as "osm"
# keeps the working OpenStreetMap setup, which needs no key.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_PROVIDER=osm
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
# Server-side key for the auth-service geocoding proxy. A separate key from the
# one above — restrict this by IP (the server), that one by HTTP referrer.
# GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_MAP_PROVIDER=osm
